# Application services

One action file exports one const. The const name is the camelCase of the kebab-case filename: `query-by-id.ts` exports `queryById`.

```ts
export interface CourseCreateCommand { name: string }

export const create = (dataSources: DataSources) => async (command: CourseCreateCommand) => {
  return dataSources.domainDataSource.Course.Course.CourseUnitOfWork.withScopedTransaction(async (repo) => {
    return repo.save(await repo.getNewInstance(command.name));
  });
};
```

- The context `index.ts` exports `interface <Name>ApplicationService` and `export const <Name> = (dataSources: DataSources, ...ports) => ({ ... })`
- Mutations (`create`, `update`, `delete`) call `withScopedTransaction`
- Queries (`query`, `get`, `find`) use `readonlyDataSource`
- Import domain and persistence ports. Do not import mongoose, mongoose models, GraphQL, or REST
- Package `src/index.ts` only hosts `ApplicationServices` and `buildApplicationServicesFactory`. New behavior goes under `contexts/`
